  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>Pakistan's Interior Minister Mohsin Naqvi extended his Tehran visit to a third day on May 18, handing Washington a revised Iranian 14-point proposal on behalf of Tehran (Reuters, AP, Pakistan Today). FM Spokesperson Esmaeil Baghaei confirmed Iran's views had been "conveyed to the American side through Pakistan" without elaborating on contents. The revision keeps nuclear discussions explicitly off the table until a permanent hostilities end is agreed, and adds demands for war-damage reparations and Hormuz sovereignty recognition — positions unchanged from Iran's April counter-offer. The Pakistan channel remains the only active conduit as neither Witkoff nor Araghchi have met directly since the April Islamabad collapse. → supports <span class="cite">F5</span> without move; moved <span class="cite">F6</span></p>

      <p>At the BRICS Foreign Ministers' meeting in New Delhi on May 14-15, FM Araghchi declared Iran had "no trust" in the US and would negotiate "only if it is serious" (Al Jazeera, Business Standard). The two-day meeting ended without a joint statement after an unnamed member — widely understood to be the UAE — blocked Iran-aligned language. Araghchi attributed the blockage to "support for Israel and the United States in their aggression against Iran." The BRICS deadlock closed off a potential multilateral pressure track that could have accelerated Pakistani-channel diplomacy. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>

      <p>On May 15, the US announced a 45-day extension of the Lebanon ceasefire after a third round of Israel-Lebanon talks in Washington (Times of Israel, Euronews, State Dept). The extension runs to late June. Within hours, the IDF launched strikes on Hezbollah infrastructure in the Harouf area and Tyre district of southern Lebanon — the first strikes since the extension was announced — killing at least six people including three paramedics (Times of Israel). IDF Chief of Staff Zamir had previously stated there "is no ceasefire" in south Lebanon. The Pentagon-convened security track is scheduled for May 29; political talks for June 2-3. → supports <span class="cite">F4</span> without move; context for <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Iran's parliament speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf declared on May 11-12 that there is "no alternative" to accepting Iran's 14-point peace proposal, warning that delay raises costs for the US (CGTN, TASS, Express Tribune). The statement, circulated through Iranian state media and confirmed by multiple wire reports, came after Trump described the ceasefire as "on life support" on May 10-11 and publicly rejected Iran's Sunday counter-proposal. Ghalibaf simultaneously warned that Iran's armed forces are "ready to give a lesson-teaching response to any aggression." → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Saudi Arabia and Kuwait lifted all restrictions on US military basing and overflight on approximately May 7-8 following a second Trump-MBS phone call, clearing the way for Project Freedom's restart (The Defense News, Cryptopolitan, House of Saud). Pentagon officials confirmed operations could resume as early as the week of May 8. Despite the restored access, Lloyd's of London stated publicly that Project Freedom did not provide "sufficient clarity or credible protection to justify resuming transits," and no major Western shipping line has announced a Hormuz return schedule. Brent crude eased to approximately $108 per barrel on May 18, down from a $114 peak, with EIA forecasting Hormuz closure through late May barring a diplomatic breakthrough. → moved <span class="cite">F5</span>; moved <span class="cite">F6</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
